Kausalyā tearfully addresses Rāma bound to his father's command --- Kausalyā laments forest alms unfit for sheltered Rāma --- Kausalyā fears burning grief and vows to follow like cow follows calf --- Rāma warns Kaikēyī-deceived king cannot survive deserted by both --- Rāma calls abandoning living husband cruel and bids serve Daśaratha --- Rāma bids both obey father as lord through fourteen forest years --- Kausalyā pleads to be led like doe amid scornful co-wives --- Rāma praises husband as god, promises Bharata's care, bids await return --- Kausalyā consents and turns to blessing rites
